+milestone: 2026.06.383
+milestone_title: "Converge the Sudoku-Extreme TRM baseline to ~0.87 with the FIXED LR schedule (4 bounded passes), THEN run the decisive verifier-as-reward graft (the LABEL de-confound never yet tested on a faithful baseline)"
+milestone_doc: openspec/change-proposals/research-roadmap-v383.md
+milestone_doc_summary: |
+  Operator directive lineage 2026-06-12/13: the LR-resume-correctness fix LANDED in .382
+  (exp4126). The nano-trm Sudoku-Extreme baseline finally ACCUMULATES: val 0.106 -> 0.278 in
+  ONE corrected-schedule pass (+0.172 vs .381's +0.01/pass = ~17x). The bottleneck is now PURELY
+  convergence wall-clock. exp4128's OWN estimate is ~4 bounded passes from 0.278 to the published
+  ~0.87, so .383 schedules FOUR accumulate passes (not 3 -- 3 would land ~0.79 and the decisive RFT
+  arm would defer a 4th time).
+
+  The Carnot verifier-as-reward graft has NEVER been tested on a FAITHFUL baseline: exp4109 (.380)
+  grafted on the interrupted 0.0232 checkpoint (not a real test); exp4119 (.381, val=0.106) and
+  exp4128 (.382, val=0.278) both honestly DEFERRED. So the central post-reframe question -- does the
+  Carnot verifier add value over the vote on a domain where it provably discriminates? -- is OPEN.
+
+  TWO design corrections from the .383 adversarial review (baked into exp4139):
+  (1) For unique-solution Sudoku the EXECUTABLE validity checker IS the oracle (passes iff candidate
+      == the unique solution). So executable-verifier rerank == oracle-vs-vote gap BY CONSTRUCTION --
+      a tautology, uninformative about the GENERAL/learned energy verifier (the product that
+      anti-discriminated on ARC grids, exp4099) and the thing DiffusionGemma's guidance actually uses.
+      Therefore the HEADLINE verifier-value signal is the NON-oracle Carnot energy/text-stat ENSEMBLE
+      rerank (the transferable verifier); the executable gap is reported SEPARATELY as a labeled
+      UPPER BOUND, never as the verifier result.
+  (2) The load-bearing, non-tautological contrast is the RFT LABEL de-confound: A=verifier-certified
+      (execution-validated-correct) vs B=vote-certified corpus, N-matched, same TRM, same pool, train
+      each, held-out exact-accuracy, CI95 excl 0. "Does verifier-certification beat vote-certification
+      as a TRAINING signal" is a real training-dynamics question even when the certifier is exact.
+
+  The graft's verifier_value_added (defined on the NON-oracle ensemble rerank AND the RFT de-confound,
+  NOT the oracle rerank) gates the queued DiffusionGemma energy-guided-diffusion scale-up
+  (docs/research-notes/diffusiongemma-energy-guided-diffusion-spec.md; GATED per 2026-06-13
+  "queued but not competing"). Mandatory oracle-vs-vote headroom positive control FIRST (oracle==vote
+  -> NO headroom -> FALSE_NEGATIVE_RISK, never "verifier fails").
+
+  ACHIEVABLE OUTCOMES (no over-promise): (a) 4 corrected-schedule passes carry val materially toward
+  0.87; (b) on a faithful (>=0.85) or near-faithful (>=0.80) baseline, the RFT LABEL de-confound +
+  the non-oracle ensemble rerank are MEASURED with CI and a headroom control -- a real verifier-value
+  verdict (positive OR honest null) rather than a 4th deferral; (c) +1 ARC level, SOTA ingested,
+  registry/hardware recorded. Any is decision-grade.
 
